From: User <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] rseq: glibc.pthread.rseq is 0 and cannot be raised

The tunable glibc.pthread.rseq has default 0 and maximum 0, so neither the
initial thread nor any new thread issues the rseq syscall, also in programs
that clear the environment; GLIBC_TUNABLES cannot raise it (the tunables
parser ignores a value above the maximum). __rseq_size is 0 and
sched_getcpu uses the getcpu syscall.

rseq is not in the Android 13 (API 33) app seccomp allowlist; the filter
traps it with SIGSYS before glibc's "registration failed" path can run.
---
--- a/sysdeps/nptl/dl-tunables.list
+++ b/sysdeps/nptl/dl-tunables.list
@@ -30,8 +30,8 @@
     rseq {
       type: INT_32
       minval: 0
-      maxval: 1
-      default: 1
+      maxval: 0
+      default: 0
     }
     stack_hugetlb {
       type: INT_32
